        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): bound Playwright response body reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n`responseBodyViaPlaywright` in the browser extension reads HTTP response bodies captured by Playwright. Previously it used `resp.text()` which loads the full response body into a JavaScript string before truncating to `maxChars`, risking OOM on large responses.\n\nChanged to prefer `resp.body()` (Buffer) with a byteLength-cap before decoding: only `maxChars * 4` bytes (UTF-8 worst-case) are decoded to string, and the existing `trimmed` slice handles any post-decode overrun.\n\n---\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n**Problem**: Browser tool response capture allocates unbounded memory when Playwright intercepts a large HTTP response. A 500 MB HTML page causes a 500 MB+ string allocation before the `maxChars` truncation check fires.\n\n**Why This Change Was Made**: `resp.text()` (string) doubles memory vs raw bytes and has no early-exit. `resp.body()` returns a Buffer, allowing byteLength inspection before string decoding. The decode window is capped at `maxChars * 4` bytes guaranteeing at least `maxChars` characters after decode (worst-case UTF-8 is 4 bytes/codepoint).\n\n**User Impact**: Reduced peak memory during browser tool response capture. Previously OOM-possible on oversized responses; now bounded to ~20 MB max.\n\n---\n\n## Root Cause\n\n**Trigger condition**: Any Playwright browser tool response where the server returns a body larger than available memory.\n\n**Root cause analysis**: `resp.text()` buffers the full response as a string. The `maxChars` check fires *after* the full string is already allocated.\n\n**Affected scope**: `extensions/browser/src/browser/pw-tools-core.responses.ts` -- all callers of `responseBodyViaPlaywright`.\n\n---\n\n## Change Summary\n\n- **Primary**: `resp.text()` -> `resp.body()` + byteLength-cap before TextDecoder\n- **Fallback**: `resp.text()` retained for the case where `resp.body` is unavailable\n- **Unchanged**: The existing `trimmed` slice still applies after decode\n\n---\n\n## Evidence\n\nFor a typical 200K-char default `maxChars`:\n\n| Metric | Before | After |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| Memory on large body | Full string (e.g., 500 MB) | Buffer + ~800 KB decoded |\n| body() unavailable | text() fallback | text() fallback (same) |\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run ...pw-tools-core.waits-next-download-saves-it\npassed (exit code 0)\n```\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (N/A -- internal impl change)\n- [ ] Breaking changes (if any) are documented in Summary (none)\n",
